The fix for crbug 573288374 (restricted: "[icu] Check memory allocation failures
in DecNum and Scale", ICU-23604, upstream ICU PR #4345): chromium/deps/icu commit
d3c612f4414600bd06a68db89944df130b5bc248, rolled into the 159 branch by 820f8b2f14
(2026-11-15). The 158 branch's DEPS pins ICU at
c670d124c9b6aa92c0b492cf543808300e0e6103, which doesn't have it.

MaybeStackArray's capacity constructor took its UErrorCode by value, so a failed
allocation was lost and callers went on with the inline (stack) buffer. DecNum's
copy constructor and setTo(), and Scale's copies, didn't check their allocations
or input lengths either (and the copy constructor copied by the source's size).
Web pages reach this code through Intl number formatting (V8 uses the bundled ICU).

This is the ICU commit's source changes (cmemory.h, number_decnum.h,
number_multiplier.cpp, number_utils.cpp) with paths under third_party/icu/; its
tests, README.chromium entry and patches/decnum_alloc_failure.patch copy are left
out. The four files are the same at c670d124 and at the commit's parent
(b09986242c), so the hunks are the commit's own. Drop this once 158's DEPS rolls
ICU to a revision that includes it.

